{"assets":[],"contestId":"285","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/285/problem/A"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"285A - Slightly Decreasing Permutations"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"As the answer you can print such permutation: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - 1, ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" + 1, 1, 2, ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, if "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 5, "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 2, then the answer is: 5, 4, 1, 2, 3. If "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"k"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" = 0, you should print 1, 2, ..., "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". Such solution can be written in two loops."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/285/problem/B"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"285B - Find Marble"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is known that a permutation can be considered as set of cycles. The integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" moves to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"p"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" (1 ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"). You can start moving from integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" along the cycle. If you find integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"t"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then print the length of the path. If you return to "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"s"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":", then print  - 1."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/285/problem/C"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"285C - Building Permutation"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The solution of the problem is rather simple. Sort all integers "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" and then make from integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[1] integer 1, from integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"[2] integer 2 and so on. So, integer "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] adds to the answer the value |"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] - "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"|. The answer should be count in 64-bit type. You can simply guess why such solution is correct."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/285/problem/D"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"285D - Permutation Sum"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For a start, describe bruteforce solution. Firstly, we will always assume, that "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" is identity permutation, that is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"a"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"["},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"] = "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"i"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":". In this case, the answer should be multiplied by "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":"!. Or in other way your bruteforce will not be counted. Secondly, using our bruteforce we can see, that for even "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" the answer is 0."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What do you also need to get accepted? First case is to calculate answers for all "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" on your computer and write them in constant array. In other words you can make precalc. Second case is to make you solution faster. The soltuion using meet-in-the-middle idea works fast for "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" ≤ 15. If you remember that for even "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"n"}],"kind":"emphasis"},{"kind":"text","text":" answer is 0 then you can get accepted using such solution. But other simple bruteforces and dynamic programmings on maps work slower than 3 seconds."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"href":"https://codeforces.com/contest/285/problem/E"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"285E - Positions in Permutations"}],"kind":"link"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"document"},"schema":2,"sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/blog/entry/7093"}